cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GoldenEye 007 PC Port — a two-agent AI development case study"
message: >-
  If you reference this project or its write-up on AI-agent collaboration,
  please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dansereau
    given-names: James
repository-code: "https://github.com/jkdansereau/goldeneye-pc-port"
abstract: >-
  A work-in-progress native PC port of GoldenEye 007 (Rare, 1997, Nintendo 64),
  built on the GoldenEye 007 decompilation, and a research project on AI-agent
  collaboration in a large, unfamiliar, low-level codebase: how two coding
  agents (a local open-weight model and a hosted frontier model), directed by
  one person part-time, were driven through ~230 translation units of unmodified
  big-endian MIPS game code and made to run on a 64-bit desktop. Covers software
  RSP emulation, N64-to-x86-64 ABI reconciliation, and a shared-artifact handoff
  workflow between agents.
keywords:
  - goldeneye-007
  - nintendo-64
  - n64
  - decompilation
